{"id": "EUVD-2026-66584", "enisaUuid": "ec157841-ac97-35fa-a927-e2eee3d2ccc4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: core: pair EH runtime PM get and put\n\nshost->eh_noresume is currently consulted twice in one error handling\niteration: once before scsi_autopm_get_host() and once again before\nscsi_autopm_put_host().\n\nThat is racy when a PM-triggered error path flips shost->eh_noresume\nwhile the SCSI EH thread is still running.\n\nThe problem flow looks like this:\nPM path\n  ufshcd_set_dev_pwr_mode()\n    shost->eh_noresume = 1\n    ufshcd_execute_start_stop  <-- trigger EH\n    ...\n    shost->eh_noresume = 0\n\nEH path\n  scsi_error_handler()\n    if (!shost->eh_noresume)\n      scsi_autopm_get_host()  <-- skipped\n    ...\n    if (!shost->eh_noresume)\n       scsi_autopm_put_host()  <-- executed later\n\nIn that case one EH iteration can skip autoresume on entry and still\ndrop a runtime PM reference on exit. That leaves an unmatched runtime PM\nput and can trigger a runtime PM usage count underflow.\n\nFix this by making eh_noresume a regular bool so it can be accessed with\nREAD_ONCE() and WRITE_ONCE(). Snapshot it once per EH iteration and use\nthat snapshot for both runtime PM get and put decisions.", "datePublished": "2026-08-26T14:37:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:46:25", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ec5f6aa38ea990af37c49af7a4bb3db00da7f9d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0038a2a75a15d163f428c93103c6d02d4d231a7a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fdc93f4a801077efbf1b87570ade8d8f325de62f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e83eed1bea142c8fe852fd53156845b88252ecd8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/872f486259ae0bc6b73ca4735a15d013241f73e9"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74754", "GHSA-5jqh-pxwf-wg8m"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01690018-34aa-326b-b2ac-ef055980df44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "06156bb9-3a88-3a7e-ba83-7ac922ac5f8d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae0751ffc77e7f21629970fdab5528c573e637f8 <0038a2a75a15d163f428c93103c6d02d4d231a7a"}, {"id": "0a6ed62d-38d0-3dfa-b468-14369f70107b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "2492970b-4d78-3b8d-ad91-a577a4eb43ab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae0751ffc77e7f21629970fdab5528c573e637f8 <872f486259ae0bc6b73ca4735a15d013241f73e9"}, {"id": "4c908526-2efc-3c3d-a0d3-d209f5810aa1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae0751ffc77e7f21629970fdab5528c573e637f8 <e83eed1bea142c8fe852fd53156845b88252ecd8"}, {"id": "71ed6752-ba48-3500-a893-28b211af3c69", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.10"}, {"id": "7497036a-7558-3eb9-ac28-c3e3762ce9af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "957a4cd1-2f43-3cf2-bb86-84587bbaab2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "c016bff2-c8ab-3a6e-ab3b-996890ef7f9c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae0751ffc77e7f21629970fdab5528c573e637f8 <1ec5f6aa38ea990af37c49af7a4bb3db00da7f9d"}, {"id": "cb500b8d-cc98-37e5-98da-a9c453a73547", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "ea5c84cf-d4f8-3f4b-8fae-17b881521547", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.3"}, {"id": "f16d3dd5-08b1-3f73-a4de-d6f769481eee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ae0751ffc77e7f21629970fdab5528c573e637f8 <fdc93f4a801077efbf1b87570ade8d8f325de62f"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "599d998e-962f-3b53-a98c-eeaf0632970b"